+                                            // anything was allocated, and looked only at
+                                            // instantaneous free heap - so every connection was
+                                            // measured against a reserve sized for exactly one.
+                                            // Two arriving together both passed, then both spent.
+                                            //
+                                            // Measured with the page already serialised to one
+                                            // fetch at a time: a browser RELOAD still produced
+                                            // conns=2, because a navigation is not a fetch and
+                                            // does not go through the client's gate. Free heap
+                                            // fell to 928, the transfer could not meet its own
+                                            // 648-byte chunk guard, and it stalled out after four
+                                            // seconds having sent nothing.
+                                            //
+                                            // MULTIPLYING BY THE CONNECTION COUNT WAS A MISTAKE,
+                                            // and it is what has been refusing reloads.
+                                            //
+                                            // "srv._heap_alloc * (openConnections.size()+1)" makes
+                                            // the requirement 2200 with none open but 3800 with one
+                                            // and 5400 with two - while free heap with a client on
+                                            // the page is only 2100-4000. So a reload arriving while
+                                            // the first connection was still listed was refused
+                                            // essentially always: 98 refusals in one capture, at
+                                            // heap 2520-3064, which the browser reports as
+                                            // ERR_CONNECTION_RESET.
