+                                            // client is only erased in __scavenge(), which runs on a
+                                            // 20-SECOND timer (H4AS_SCAVENGE_FREQ), so a socket the
+                                            // browser closed a moment ago still counts against the
+                                            // next one for up to twenty seconds. The gate was
+                                            // charging full price for corpses.
+                                            //
+                                            // A flat reserve is the honest version: the page is
+                                            // serialised to one request at a time, so the case the
+                                            // multiplier was built for - several arriving together -
+                                            // is already prevented on the client. Concurrency that
+                                            // the client cannot control (captive-portal probes) is
+                                            // better handled by failing one request than by locking
+                                            // everything out.
                                             auto _heapLO = H4AT_HEAP_THROTTLE_LO + srv._heap_alloc;
                                             // auto _heapHI = H4AT_HEAP_THROTTLE_HI + srv._heap_alloc;
                                             auto _blockLO= H4AT_HEAP_THROTTLE_LO + srv._block_alloc;
